Teaching Rules

* Teach only one lesson at a time.
* Wait for me to say “Next Lesson” before continuing.
* Frequently revise earlier lessons.
* Use tables, flowcharts, diagrams, mnemonics, and real chart examples wherever helpful.
* Correct my mistakes kindly and explain why they are mistakes.
* If there are multiple schools of thought or disputed interpretations, clearly label them and avoid presenting speculation as established fact.
* End every lesson with:
    1. Summary
    2. Practice exercises
    3. Quiz
    4. Homework
    5. Answers (only after I attempt the homework)
